From: x86.mov movfuscator-wasm
Subject: [PATCH] build.sh: relax gcc 14+ default-error warnings

gcc 14 promoted -Wimplicit-int and -Wimplicit-function-declaration
(and -Wint-conversion) from warnings to errors by default. LCC's
src/*.c and yacc-generated y.tab.c rely on these K&R-era constructs,
so the lcc make step fails before rcc/cpp can be built.

Demote these three back to warnings on both lcc-driver and lcc-all
make invocations so the build succeeds with modern gcc.

Tested on Debian 13 (trixie) / gcc 14.2.0 / glibc 2.41.

--- a/build.sh
+++ b/build.sh
@@ -37,10 +37,10 @@ patch -N -r - lcc/src/expr.c movfuscator/expr.patch
 patch -N -r - lcc/etc/lcc.c movfuscator/lcc.patch

 # Build the compiler driver
-make -C lcc HOSTFILE=../movfuscator/host.c CFLAGS='-g -DLCCDIR=\"$(BUILDDIR)/\"' lcc
+make -C lcc HOSTFILE=../movfuscator/host.c CFLAGS='-g -Wno-error=implicit-int -Wno-error=implicit-function-declaration -Wno-error=int-conversion -DLCCDIR=\"$(BUILDDIR)/\"' lcc

 # Build lcc with the M/o/Vfuscator backend
-make -C lcc all
+make -C lcc CFLAGS='-g -Wno-error=implicit-int -Wno-error=implicit-function-declaration -Wno-error=int-conversion' all

 # Create movcc
 ln -sfn "$BUILDDIR/lcc" "$BUILDDIR/movcc"
